# WoW client artefacts
*.bak
*.old
WTF/
Interface/

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local design reference — not part of the distributed addon
design_handoff_heroPanel/

# Author-side notes and tooling — not part of the distributed addon and of no
# use to a player installing it. Kept locally, deliberately untracked.
#
# tools/* rather than tools/, because git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded. package.py is the exception: cutting a release has to
# be reproducible by whoever does it next, so the build script is versioned even
# though the rest of the directory is not.
CLAUDE.md
TESTING.md
tools/*
!tools/package.py

# Research notes written while building a feature. Working documents: they
# record where data came from and what was ruled out, which is worth keeping
# locally and is not part of what a player installs.
*-research-and-prompt*.md

# Packaging output. The zips are build artefacts - derivable from the tag they
# are attached to, and distributed as release assets rather than from the repo.
# release/notes.md is deliberately *not* ignored: it is authored prose, the same
# kind of source as the README, and it wants a history and a diff before it is
# published.
/dist/
*.zip

# Test harness dependencies
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Python bytecode from the glyph generator
__pycache__/
*.pyc
